This will pass if the "New_Ret" is negative, which is expected based on the description under the comment. Please adjust your assertion accordingly according to the exact comments provided or your need.--------------------The following C# code uses the `Debug.Assert` statement to check the relationship between the last index of the element `x` in the old array and the new array. 

```cs

public void PUT_IndexOfContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int x)
{
    int Old_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);
    
    int New_Ret = arrList.IndexOf(x);

    int New_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);

    Debug.Assert(New_Ret >= (Old_arrListLastIndexOfX == -1 ? -1 : Old_arrListLastIndexOfX), "Invalid Last Index Of 'X'");
    Debug.Assert(New_Ret == (New_arrListLastIndexOfX == -1 ? -1 : New_arrListLastIndexOfX), "Invalid Last Index Of 'X'");           
}
```

This code will throw an `AssertionException` if the new index contains a different last index of `x` from the old index.--------------------So, in C#, we can check if a value is negative using the `<` operator. And we can check the last index of an item in a collection using the `LastIndexOf()` method which returns -1 if the item doesn't exist. Below is the assertion:

```cs
// Assert
Debug.Assert(
    Old_arrListLastIndexOfX == -1 && New_Ret == -1,
    "If the return value is negative, last index of x in old array is -1"
);
```

This assertion will pass if the `Old_arrListLastIndexOfX` is also -1, the value that `IndexOf()` returns is -1.--------------------```cs

namespace ArrayList.Test
{
    public partial class ArrayListContractTest
    {
        public void PUT_IndexOfContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int x)
        {
            AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(true);

            int Old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
            int Old_x = x;
            int Old_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);
            bool Old_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

            int New_Ret = arrList.IndexOf(x);

            Debug.Assert(New_Ret < 0 || New_Ret == arrList.LastIndexOf(x));  // If the return value is negative, last index of x in old array is -1   

            int New_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
            int New_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);
            bool New_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList_Count", Old_arrListCount);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$new_arrList_Count", New_arrListCount);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList_x", Old_x);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList_LastIndexOf_x", Old_arrListLastIndexOfX);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$new_arrList_LastIndexOf_x", New_arrListLastIndexOfX);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$New_ret", New_Ret);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$old_arrList_contains_x", Old_arrListContainsX);
            PexObserve.ValueForViewing("$new_arrList_contains_x", New_arrListContainsX);
        }
    }
}

```

